silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_freesigma_enc__sigma_enc_algebra_a__alpha__!_a__ev_free a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Free(Sigma_enc) is the carrier of the initial Sigma_enc-algebra: the set of all finite Sigma_enc-trees over the publish signature. A Sigma_enc-algebra is a pair (A, alpha) where A is a set and alpha is a Sigma_enc-action alpha : Sigma_enc(A) -> A telling A how to absorb each summand. !_A is the unique algebra-morphism (catamorphism / fold) from the initial algebra to any other algebra. ev_Free : Sigma_enc(Free) -> Free is the structure map of the initial algebra (an iso by Lambek lemma)." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_catamorphism___structural_recursion___fold a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The operation !_A is defined by structural recursion on Sigma_enc-trees: for a leaf eta(r) with r in RawSource, !_A(eta(r)) = the raw embedding into A; for an inner node tagged stage_i with children, !_A(node) = alpha_i(!_A on children). The defining commuting square is alpha o Sigma_enc(!_A) = !_A o ev_Free: applying alpha after lifting !_A through Sigma_enc equals !_A on the structure map. By initiality, this !_A is unique." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_initial_algebra__catamorphism__lambek_lemma a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats Section 20.4 (free monad on a signature endofunctor; initial algebras of polynomial signatures) is the categorical base topic. Adamek-Trnkova 1990 supplies the transfinite construction of initial algebras. Lambek 1968 proves the structure map of the initial algebra is an isomorphism. Meijer-Fokkinga-Paterson 1991 (Functional Programming with Bananas, Lenses, Envelopes and Barbed Wire, FPCA) supplies the catamorphism fold as the canonical recursive evaluation." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_mereology_algebra_paper_19__mittens_publish_tree_fold a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The concrete anchor: paper-19 supplies the mereology algebra (Mereo, alpha_19) where alpha_19 absorbs each Sigma_enc-summand into a mereology operation: alpha_19_raw embeds raw rows as atomic parts; alpha_19_custody glues parts under custody; alpha_19_type glues parts under typing; alpha_19_admit glues parts under admission. The unique morphism !_19 : Free(Sigma_enc) -> Mereo evaluates every Sigma_enc-tree as one mereology term. Paper-19 does NOT redefine Sigma_enc; it picks an algebra and lets initiality do the work." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_unique_mediator_profile__homfreesigma_enc__a_iso_algebra_str a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda-style profile of the initial algebra: Hom_{Alg(Sigma_enc)}(Free(Sigma_enc), (A, alpha)) is a singleton for every Sigma_enc-algebra (A, alpha); the unique element is !_A. Every downstream encyclopedia paper inherits this property: paper-19 mereology has !_19; paper-15 KG-growth has !_15; paper-25 sheaf-gluing has !_25; each is the unique catamorphism into that paper's chosen algebra. The Yoneda profile of Free(Sigma_enc) in Alg(Sigma_enc) is the constant terminal singleton." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_decomposition_step__step_initial_algebra_theorem_recap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Free(Sigma_enc) is the initial Sigma_enc-algebra; every algebra (A, alpha) receives a unique algebra-morphism !_A given by structural recursion; the commuting square alpha o Sigma_enc(!_A) = !_A o ev_Free expresses initiality. Every downstream encyclopedia paper inherits one unique catamorphism into its chosen target algebra; paper-19 mereology is the canonical concrete case." .
